 if len(files)==4:
  meta={'id':ASSET,'version':'1.0.0','category':'props','assetKind':'prop','theme':'culture','style':'S01-clean-geometric','title':TITLE,'description':'One newly authored complete molinillo-inspired static wooden-look chocolate-stirrer exterior. One entire continuous body joins a broad eight-scalloped end head, narrow neck, integral retaining shoulders and a long slender turned grip with two shallow dark recessed bands. Three independent whole annular rings surround the short neck above the carved head; each true through-bore retains visible upper air around the narrow shaft and sits in a deliberate fixed overlap on its complete shoulder. Four closed editable whole meshes and four opaque constant PBR roles, metres native Z up, whole horizontal bounds centred with a finite lower head sole as the upright display datum. All numeric profiles, eight head grooves, shoulders and ring sections are new, not a cabasa beaded cylinder with recoloured loops, a twin cage geared hand beater, honey dipper or extracted cooking accessory. One model zero scenes. Broad Mexican craft-tool category inspiration only; no particular artisan work, inscriptions, ornamental carving or historical replica. Rings are fixed in this static pose, not free-spinning or mechanically captive under motion; no actual wood species, internal grain, chocolate, beverage, food contact, mixing/frothing result, preparation instructions, grip fit, rotation, sound, balance, manufacturing or safety capability claimed. No rig, animation or interaction.','bounds':dict(zip(['x','y','z'],[hi[k]-lo[k]for k in range(3)]),unit='m'),'triangles':triangle_count,'materials':4,'files':files,'status':'review','license':'All rights reserved'}
